From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: append the u_trace of earlier secondary VMR segments
 biblioklept

CmdExecuteCommands appended the secondary's u_trace only when the
secondary's last CS stream was non-empty. A secondary whose
cmd_cut_vmr_segment cut left a subqueue stream empty after the last
cut (all its work in earlier segments) still had its earlier segments
called, but their trace events (the u_trace is not cut per segment)
were never appended to the primary.

Append once per subqueue after the last call into it, when either the
final stream or any earlier segment was called.

Build-only; not device-tested.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c |   10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
index 61fe19f..659cfd6 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -1311,7 +1311,17 @@ panvk_per_arch(CmdExecuteCommands)(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
             cs_move32_to(prim_b, size, cs_root_chunk_size(sec_b));
             cs_call(prim_b, addr, size);
             prim_b->req_resource_mask |= sec_b->req_resource_mask;
+         }
 
+         /* The secondary's u_trace covers every segment (cmd_cut_vmr_segment
+          * does not cut it): append it once, after the last call into this
+          * subqueue, also when the last segment is empty and only the
+          * earlier ones were called. */
+         bool called = !cs_is_empty(sec_b);
+         for (uint32_t s = 0; s < seg_count && !called; s++)
+            called = segs[s].size[j] != 0;
+         if (called) {
+            struct cs_builder *prim_b = panvk_get_cs_builder(primary, j);
             struct u_trace *prim_ut = &primary->utrace.uts[j];
             struct u_trace *sec_ut = &secondary->utrace.uts[j];
             u_trace_clone_append(u_trace_begin_iterator(sec_ut),
